The examples in this directory are described in the userguide, except for
couette1a and couette1b.

Short description
-----------------

couette1:

 Viscoelastic problem on a unit square
 linear Couette flow
 DEVSS-G/SUPG
 first-order time integration

couette1a:

 Viscoelastic problem on a unit square
 linear Couette flow
 DEVSS-G/SUPG
 first-order time integration

 This is the couette1 problem with the following changes:
  1) Q1isoQ2 shape functions
  2) subdomain Gauss integration (using 4 subdomains)

couette1b:

 Viscoelastic problem on a unit square
 linear Couette flow
 DEVSS-G/SUPG
 first-order time integration

 This is the couette1 problem with the following changes:
  1) triangular elements
  2) P1isoP2 shape functions
  3) subdomain Gauss integration (using 4 subdomains/subtriangles)

couette2:

 Viscoelastic problem on a unit square
 linear Couette flow
 DEVSS-G/SUPG
 second-order time integration

couette3:

 Viscoelastic problem on a unit square
 linear Couette flow
 DEVSS-G/SUPG
 Implicit bilinear terms of CE in momentum balance.
 first-order time integration

couette4:

 Viscoelastic problem on a unit square
 linear Couette flow
 DEVSS-G/SUPG
 Implicit bilinear terms of CE in momentum balance.
 second-order time integration

couette5:

 Viscoelastic problem on a unit square
 linear Couette flow
 DEVSS-G/SUPG
 second-order time integration
 two viscoelastic modes

couette6:

 Viscoelastic problem on a unit square
 linear Couette flow
 DEVSS-G/SUPG
 Implicit bilinear terms of CE in momentum balance.
 first-order time integration
 two viscoelastic modes

couette7:

 Viscoelastic problem on a unit square
 linear Couette flow
 DEVSS/DG
 first-order time integration

couette8:

 Viscoelastic problem on a unit square
 linear Couette flow
 DEVSS/DG
 second-order time integration

couette9:

 Viscoelastic problem on a unit square
 linear Couette flow
 DEVSS-G/SUPG
 Implicit bilinear terms of CE in momentum balance.
 L2-projection of c=exp(s) on the finite element approximation space in the
 momentum balance.
 second-order time integration
 NOTE: this is similar to couette4, but now using the L2-projection of
       c=exp(s).

couette10:

 Viscoelastic problem on a unit square
 linear Couette flow
 G/SUPG
 second-order time integration
 NOTE: similar to couette2, but omitting DEVSS.

couette11:

 Viscoelastic problem on a unit square
 linear Couette flow
 G/SUPG
 Implicit bilinear terms of CE in momentum balance.
 second-order time integration
 NOTE: similar to couette4, but omitting DEVSS.

couette12:

 Viscoelastic problem on a unit square
 linear Couette flow
 G/SUPG
 first-order time integration
 NOTE: similar to couette1, but omitting DEVSS.

couette13:

 Viscoelastic problem on a unit square
 linear Couette flow
 G/SUPG
 Implicit bilinear terms of CE in momentum balance.
 first-order time integration
 NOTE: similar to couette3, but omitting DEVSS.

couette14:

 Linear Couette flow for an integral UCM model.
 Problem 1:
   Poiseuille flow on a unit square. Periodical boundary conditions.
   Collocation of nodes.
   Stress-implicit formulation of the momentum balance.
 Problem 2: Deformation fields computed as a function of time, assuming the
   a steady state initial condition for the fields.
 Problem 3: Stress tensor projection on the interpolation space for F.
 Implicit DG with P1 or P2 interpolation for tau-convection.
 Extrapolated BDF2 time discretization.

couette15, couette15a:

 Viscoelastic problem on a unit square using b-formulation.
 linear Couette flow
 DEVSS-G/SUPG
 Implicit bilinear terms of CE in momentum balance.
 L2-projection of c=b.b^T on the finite element approximation space in the
 momentum balance.
 second-order time integration
 NOTE: This is similar to couette9, but now using the b-formulation.
 NOTE: To find the reference steady state conformation tensor, the flow is
       first run starting from the exact steady state without an imposed
       disturbance until timestep dist_step.
 NOTE: couette15 uses nodal point level rotation reinitialization.
       couette15a uses element level rotation reinitialization.

couette16, couette16a:

 Viscoelastic problem on a unit square using b-formulation
 Explicit div tau term.
 linear Couette flow
 DEVSS-G/SUPG
 second-order time integration
 NOTE: This is similar to couette2, but now using the b-formulation.
 NOTE: To find the reference steady state conformation tensor, the flow is
       first run starting from the exact steady state without an imposed
       disturbance until timestep dist_step.
 NOTE: couette16 uses nodal point level rotation reinitialization.
       couette16a uses element level rotation reinitialization.

couette17:

 Viscoelastic problem on a unit square
 linear Couette flow
 DEVSS-G/SUPG
 second-order time integration
 Fully-implicit with Newton-Raphson for the conformation tensor.
 NOTE: Similar to couette2, but now with implicit conformation.

couette18:

 Viscoelastic problem on a unit square
 linear Couette flow
 DEVSS-G/SUPG
 Implicit bilinear terms of CE in momentum balance.
 L2-projection of c=exp(s) on the finite element approximation space in the
 momentum balance.
 second-order time integration
 Fully-implicit with Newton-Raphson for the conformation tensor.
 NOTE: Similar to couette9, but now with implicit conformation.

couette19:

 Viscoelastic problem on a unit square
 linear Couette flow
 DEVSS-G/SUPG
 second-order time integration
 Fully-implicit with Newton-Raphson for the b-tensor.
 NOTE: To find the reference steady state conformation tensor, the flow is
       first run starting from the exact steady state without an imposed
       disturbance until timestep dist_step.
 NOTE: This is similar to couette2, but now using the b-formulation with
       implicit b-tensor.
 NOTE: couette19 uses nodal point level rotation reinitialization.
       couette19a uses element level rotation reinitialization.

couette20:

 Viscoelastic problem on a unit square using b-formulation.
 linear Couette flow
 DEVSS-G/SUPG
 Implicit bilinear terms of CE in momentum balance.
 L2-projection of c=b.b^T on the finite element approximation space in the
 momentum balance.
 second-order time integration
 Fully-implicit with Newton-Raphson for the b-tensor.
 NOTE: To find the reference steady state conformation tensor, the flow is
       first run starting from the exact steady state without an imposed
       disturbance until timestep dist_step.
 NOTE: This is similar to couette15, but now with implicit b-tensor.
 NOTE: couette20 uses nodal point level rotation reinitialization.
       couette20a uses element level rotation reinitialization.

couette21:

 Viscoelastic problem on a unit square (c formulation)
 linear Couette flow
 DEVSS-G/SUPG
 second-order time integration
 Fully-implicit with Newton-Raphson
 Optionally include Jacobian of SUPG test function.
 NOTE: Similar to couette2, but now fully implicit

couette22, couette22a:

 Viscoelastic problem on a unit square (b formulation)
 linear Couette flow
 DEVSS-G/SUPG
 second-order time integration
 Fully-implicit with Newton-Raphson
 Optionally include Jacobian of SUPG test function.
 NOTE: To find the reference steady state conformation tensor, the flow is
       first run starting from the exact steady state without an imposed
       disturbance until timestep dist_step.
 NOTE: Similar to couette15, but now fully implicit
 NOTE: couette22 uses nodal point level rotation reinitialization.
       couette22a uses element level rotation reinitialization.

couette23:

 Viscoelastic problem on a unit square (c formulation)
 linear Couette flow
 DEVSS-G/SUPG
 Building generalized eigenvalue problem
    (A-lambda B)v = 0
 for linear stability analysis.
 Both A and B have the same non-zero matrix structure.
 FEAST eigenvalue solver.

couette24:

 Viscoelastic problem on a unit square (c formulation)
 linear Couette flow
 DEVSS-G/SUPG
 Building generalized eigenvalue problem
    (A-lambda B)v = 0
 for linear stability analysis.
 Matrices A and B have a different non-zero matrix structure.
 FEAST eigenvalue solver.

couette25:

 Viscoelastic problem on a unit square (b formulation)
 linear Couette flow
 DEVSS-G/SUPG
 Building generalized eigenvalue problem
    (A-lambda B)v = 0
 for linear stability analysis.
 Both A and B have the same non-zero matrix structure.
 FEAST eigenvalue solver.
 NOTE: Similar to couette23, but now using the b-formulation.

couette26:

 Viscoelastic problem on a unit square (b formulation)
 linear Couette flow
 DEVSS-G/SUPG
 Building generalized eigenvalue problem
    (A-lambda B)v = 0
 for linear stability analysis.
 Matrices A and B have a different non-zero matrix structure.
 FEAST eigenvalue solver.
 NOTE: Similar to couette24, but now using the b-formulation.

couette27

 Viscoelastic problem on a unit square (b formulation)
 linear Couette flow
 DEVSS-G/SUPG
 second-order time integration
 Fully-implicit with Newton-Raphson
 Optionally include Jacobian of SUPG test function.
 Optionally use L=G or L=(nabla u)^T in constitutive equation.
 NOTE: To find the reference steady state b-tensor, the flow is
       first solved for the exact steady state without an imposed
       disturbance using Newton-Raphson.
 NOTE: This is similar to couette22a, but now using Newton-Raphson iteration to
       find the steady state first instead of time-stepping.
